IMPORTANT: SPX_SHA256_ADDR_BYTES = 22 (not 32). The SHA2 backend uses 22-byte addresses.

IMPORTANT: In hash_sha2.c, the hash_message function computes SPX_INBLOCKS:
```c
#define SPX_INBLOCKS (((SPX_N + SPX_PK_BYTES + SPX_SHAX_BLOCK_BYTES - 1) & -SPX_SHAX_BLOCK_BYTES) / SPX_SHAX_BLOCK_BYTES)
```
This rounds up (SPX_N + SPX_PK_BYTES) to the nearest multiple of the block size.

