    pub buf: [u8; 128],
}
```

Constants: cst[16] are 64-bit values.
padding[129] = [0x80, 0, 0, ...]
ROT is `((x << (64-n)) | (x >> n))` for 64-bit.
Block size is 128 bytes, datalen in bits.

IMPORTANT: In blake512.c, the `cst` array is declared as `const u64 cst[16]` (NOT static). This is the same name as in blake256.c but different values. In Rust, use different names like CST256 and CST512.

