The haraka.c file is very large (26127 bytes). Here is a summary of its structure:

### haraka.c - Bit-sliced AES-based Haraka implementation

This implements Haraka-256 and Haraka-512 using a constant-time bit-sliced AES implementation.

Key constants:
- HARAKAS_RATE = 32
- haraka512_rc64[10][8] - Round constants for Haraka-512 (10 rounds, 8 u64 values each)

Key helper functions (all internal/static):
- br_dec32le(src) - Load u32 little-endian
- br_range_dec32le(v, num, src) - Load array of u32 LE
- br_enc32le(dst, x) - Store u32 little-endian
- br_range_enc32le(dst, v, num) - Store array of u32 LE
- br_aes_ct64_bitslice_Sbox(q: &mut [u64; 8]) - AES S-box on bit-sliced state
- br_aes_ct64_bitslice_invSbox(q: &mut [u64; 8]) - Inverse AES S-box (not used in Haraka, but present)
- br_aes_ct64_ortho(q: &mut [u64; 8]) - Orthogonalize bit-sliced state
- br_aes_ct64_interleave_in(q0, q1, w: &[u32; 4]) - Interleave 128-bit block into bit-sliced form
- br_aes_ct64_interleave_out(w: &mut [u32; 4], q0, q1) - De-interleave
- br_aes_ct64_shiftrows(q: &mut [u64; 8]) - AES ShiftRows
- br_aes_ct64_mixcolumns(q: &mut [u64; 8]) - AES MixColumns

Key public functions:
- tweak_constants(ctx) - Tweaks the round constants with the public seed
  This XORs the pub_seed into the round constants and applies Haraka-512 permutation
  to produce tweaked512_rc64 and tweaked256_rc32 stored in ctx.

- haraka512_perm(out, in, ctx) - Applies 512-bit Haraka permutation (5 rounds of AES)
- haraka512(out, in, ctx) - Haraka-512: permutation then XOR with input, output first 32 bytes
- haraka256(out, in, ctx) - Haraka-256: similar but for 256-bit input

- haraka_S_inc_init(s_inc) - Init sponge state (65 bytes: 32 state + 32 rate + 1 position)
- haraka_S_inc_absorb(s_inc, m, mlen, ctx) - Absorb into sponge
- haraka_S_inc_finalize(s_inc) - Finalize sponge (pad)
- haraka_S_inc_squeeze(out, outlen, s_inc, ctx) - Squeeze from sponge
- haraka_S(out, outlen, in, inlen, ctx) - Non-incremental sponge

The sponge uses HARAKAS_RATE=32 and the Haraka-512 permutation as the underlying function.
The state is 64 bytes (512 bits), with rate=32 bytes.

IMPORTANT DETAILS about the sponge:
- s_inc is 65 bytes: bytes 0..63 are the state, byte 64 is the position counter
- haraka_S_inc_absorb XORs message bytes into state at position s_inc[64]
- When position reaches HARAKAS_RATE (32), apply haraka512_perm to the state
- haraka_S_inc_finalize pads with 0x1f at current position and 0x80 at position 31
- haraka_S_inc_squeeze outputs bytes from the state starting at position (HARAKAS_RATE - s_inc[64])

IMPORTANT: The tweak_constants function is complex:
1. It takes the 10 round constants (haraka512_rc64[10][8]) and XORs pub_seed into them
2. Then applies haraka512_perm to each pair of round constant rows
3. Stores results in ctx.tweaked512_rc64 and derives ctx.tweaked256_rc32

The bit-sliced AES implementation works on 8 uint64_t values representing 8 bits of 64 parallel AES states. The S-box is implemented as a Boolean circuit.

For the AES round in Haraka:
1. Load 4 128-bit blocks into bit-sliced form (interleave)
2. XOR with round constants
3. Apply S-box
4. Apply ShiftRows
5. Apply MixColumns
6. De-interleave back to normal form

The haraka512_perm function does 5 rounds of this, with a specific mixing pattern between rounds.

Please read the C source file at c_src/lib/haraka/src/haraka.c carefully and translate it faithfully. The bit-sliced operations must be exact for byte-identical output.

### hash_haraka.c
- initialize_hash_function: calls tweak_constants(ctx)
- prf_addr: haraka512(outbuf, addr || sk_seed_padded_to_32, ctx), output SPX_N bytes
  NOTE: buf is 64 bytes, first 32 = addr, next SPX_N = sk_seed, rest = 0
- gen_message_random: sponge absorb sk_prf || optrand || m, squeeze SPX_N bytes
- hash_message: sponge absorb R || pk_root || m, squeeze SPX_DGST_BYTES, parse digest/tree/leaf
  NOTE: Only absorbs pk + SPX_N (the root part), not the full pk

### thash_haraka_simple.c (cfg(feature = "simple"))
- thash with inblocks==1: haraka512(outbuf, addr_padded || input_padded, ctx)
  buf_tmp is 64 bytes: first 32 = addr, next SPX_N = input, rest = 0
- thash with inblocks>1: haraka_S(out, SPX_N, addr || input, SPX_ADDR_BYTES + inblocks*SPX_N, ctx)

### thash_haraka_robust.c (cfg(feature = "robust"))
- thash with inblocks==1:
  1. haraka256(outbuf, addr_padded, ctx) to get bitmask
  2. XOR input with bitmask
  3. haraka512(outbuf, addr_padded || xored_input, ctx)
- thash with inblocks>1:
  1. haraka_S(bitmask, inblocks*SPX_N, addr, SPX_ADDR_BYTES, ctx)
  2. XOR input with bitmask
  3. haraka_S(out, SPX_N, addr || xored_input, SPX_ADDR_BYTES + inblocks*SPX_N, ctx)

